⚠️ N4 ABORTED ON ITS FIRST ATTEMPT and the abort is recorded rather than edited
out. Its guard was `grep -q '20260408113029_cron_heartbeat' scripts/lint-app-guc.mjs`,
which still matched because the script's own doc comment names that migration
twice — so the guard reported "MUTATION DID NOT APPLY" for a mutation that HAD
applied. The harness restored from the byte backup and exited 1 rather than
running an unguarded assertion. The guard was re-cut to count ALLOWLIST ENTRIES
(`^    file: \`\${MIGRATIONS_DIR}/`) and re-run, which is the reading above. A
guard that matches prose is the same class of defect as an assertion that matches
prose.


